WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.347
What is a relief?.

2
00:00:01.507 --> 00:00:04.897
A relief is a picture that stands out from a flat surface.

3
00:00:05.057 --> 00:00:07.054
Some parts are raised, standing up.

4
00:00:07.214 --> 00:00:09.350
Some are pressed in, sinking down.

5
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.414
The head on a coin is a relief.

6
00:00:12.114 --> 00:00:13.275
Raised parts.

7
00:00:13.435 --> 00:00:17.197
To make a raised part, add a clay shape on top of the tile.

8
00:00:17.357 --> 00:00:20.515
Score and slip it, so it stays on when the clay dries.

9
00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:23.925
Raised parts catch the light and throw small shadows.

10
00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:25.926
Pressed-in marks.

11
00:00:26.086 --> 00:00:28.919
Press tools into the soft clay to make textures.

12
00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:30.890
A fork makes lines like fur.

13
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.675
A pencil end makes dots.

14
00:00:32.835 --> 00:00:35.621
A shell makes curved ridges, like fish scales.

15
00:00:36.321 --> 00:00:37.390
Picture bricks.

16
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:46.791
About two thousand years ago, in Han dynasty China, people made clay bricks with pictures of everyday life: horses, carts, farmers and markets.

17
00:00:46.951 --> 00:00:49.273
Many were pressed from carved moulds.
